SM(366,{"n":"Numbers 18","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Numbers 18.mp3","d":2097.9,"s":[[0.32,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[9.04,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[23.52,"Okay, we'll go ahead and get started."],[26.32,"When we get started, we're gonna be picking up at the beginning of Numbers chapter 18."],[31.76,"Continue our way through the exciting book of Numbers."],[34.8,"More exciting than people thought going in, I bet."],[37.36,"That's true. But that was a low bar for some folks, I think."],[41.28,"Um so once again tonight, we're not gonna have a ton of introduction, because once again, tonight, we're shifting gears."],[50.34,"One of the reasons we left off where we left off is that we're moving from one type of content to another type of uh content again."],[57.94,"So we last time talked about Korra's Rebellion and the fallout from that, the plague, the censors, all that good stuff."],[67.18,"And the stuff we're gonna talk about tonight is not unrelated, but it's a different type of text."],[75.98,"So that was narrative."],[77.42,"We were reading a series of stories, and those stories were about due to Korra's rebellion, and I made my usual Korra is the first Protestant joke because he says, you know, are we not all holy?"],[89.9,"Why are you trying to make yourself a priest over us?"],[92.54,"Um, but it got the same reaction last time, too."],[95.98,"People just don't think that joke's funny, I guess."],[97.98,"Won't stop me."],[99.34,"So, and then through several means, of course, one of those means being the ground swallowing Korah hole, uh, and some other things, and then ultimately through uh the budding of Aaron's rod."],[113.38,"We're talking about the end of last time, it is sort of firmly established that no, this is authority as high priest that's been given to Aaron, but it's been given to him by God."],[122.9,"This is not a responsibility he took for himself."],[126.34,"This is not him trying to lord it over people."],[128.5,"He did not seize it, no one can seize it."],[131.46,"The only way to legitimately have this authority is for God to give it to you."],[135.46,"And so that has now been firmly displayed."],[138.5,"That said, what we're now going to talk about is we're gonna review some of the duties of the priests and the Levites."],[145.62,"So we're gonna be talking about some of the responsibilities that come with that authority."],[149.22,"So what we're going to talk about tonight is not unrelated to what we just talked about"],[153.58,"It's connected, but it's also a different, we're not reading narrative anymore."],[158.72,"We're not progressing the story."],[160.24,"And it's important to keep in mind that we're not getting any kind of real time narration here, remember?"],[166.32,"Just a few chapters ago, we had God telling the people that they were going to spend the next 40 years wandering in the wilderness until the generation that came out of Egypt dies off."],[179.04,"And in a few chapters, when we get to the end of numbers, it's going to be 40 years later."],[185.96,"So when we have these shifts and we shift back to narrative, it's not picking up where it left off."],[192.92,"We get a series of windows here in numbers to specific important events that take place over the course of that 40 years."],[203.84,"But there's whole years where we're not given any inkling as to all the things that happened."],[210.18,"But that also means we have to keep in mind that there's this whole life of the people and the community and all of these things going on all the time."],[217.64,"All through these 40 years, and those are punctuated by these sort of major, significant major events."],[225.72,"So uh that said, by way of review, a quick review, uh, unless we have any leftover questions or comments or musings about fairies as they appear. in the works of various people"],[239.6,"We'll go ahead and pick up in uh Numbers chapter 18, verse 1."],[245.6,"Now the Lord spoke to Aaron saying, You and your sons and your father's house with you shall bear the sins of the holy things, and you and your sons with you shall bear the sins of your priesthood."],[257.68,"Okay, pause. This means they're gonna be punished for it."],[261.33,"So the reason I keep making this point is there are other passages and other texts in the Old Testament that some of our friends read and to just assume that the language means a certain thing, because that's what it sounds like in English."],[278.53,"Okay. So they're gonna go to like Isaiah 53, where it talks about the servant pointing to Christ bearing our sins."],[288.57,"And they're gonna assume that that means certain things."],[292.91,"They're gonna assume that that means certain things."],[296.03,"But there are plenty of other places in the Old Testament where this language is used, like here in the Torah, where that same language is used, where what they read into that other passage doesn't make a lick of sense."],[308.23,"So when they talk about Isaiah 53, they're gonna say, oh, well, that means that God punished Jesus for our sins."],[315.35,"That's what bearing our sins means."],[318.28,"Well, okay, so does this mean that Aaron and his family are gonna be punished for the sins of the objects in the tabernacle?"],[324.6,"Does that make any sense"],[328.88,"And they're gonna be they're they're gonna bear those sins, and they're gonna bear their own sins."],[336.18,"So they're gonna get like double punished, but some of the sins they're gonna be punished for are the sins of inanimate objects."],[344.91,"Obviously, that doesn't make sense."],[346.43,"But now remember what we talked about back in Leviticus chapter 16, many moons ago."],[351.79,"We have a very different understanding of sin than the understanding of sin that the Torah puts forward, and that's say St."],[358.11,"Paul uses. When we hear sin, we think of the idea that's usually more connoted by the idea of a trespass"],[366.49,"When we hear sin, we think, oh, breaking a rule."],[369.89,"There was a rule, you're not supposed to do this, or you are supposed to do this, and you either did it or didn't do it, depending on which one you weren't supposed to do."],[378.38,"You did the wrong thing."],[379.42,"And so now you're guilty of it, and you're since you broke the rule and you're guilty of breaking the rule, you're now liable to punishment."],[386.46,"Some kind of punishment for having broken the rule."],[389.1,"That's how we think about it."],[390.78,"That's not the Bible, to be blunt."],[395.18,"That's not what sin is, that's not how it works in the Bible."],[399.42,"Sin is talked about in the Bible as a force that's active in the world."],[406.62,"Remember all the way back in Genesis chapter 4 with Cain and Abel."],[411.72,"God comes to Cain and says, Sin is crouching at your door."],[414.76,"It wants to master you."],[416.2,"You must master it."],[418.52,"He doesn't mean breaking a rule is crouching at your door."],[422.7,"That doesn't make any sense."],[424.22,"It's this force, it's this power that's at work in the world."],[427.1,"Now, this is sin's plural."],[429.26,"And so sin's plural, that's the effects."],[433.74,"If sin is the disease, then sins are the symptoms."],[438.16,"Of that disease."],[440.16,"And so if you think about sin as like a spore."],[445.42,"As like germs, even though they didn't have the germ theory of disease, it was more like spore."],[450.22,"But you understand."],[451.16,"Objects can be contaminated."],[453.08,"Certain diseases. spread"],[455.12,"A person has this disease, you have to take their blanket and burn it, because you have to take their possessions and burn them."],[461.68,"You have to clear things out of that."],[463.5,"And that's the two examples that are used are always plague, disease, and then on the other side, mildew or mold."],[471.26,"Which again gets into things and spreads."],[476.14,"And so it's not that the candlest hand in the tabernacle or the altar broke a rule somehow."],[485.02,"But it can get tainted by the sinful people, like the priests themselves."],[492.88,"Their own sins."],[494.4,"The priests themselves are not infected with sin. and commit sins and manifest these symptoms"],[500.92,"And they're coming in to the tabernacle and using these things and handling these things, over the course of their ministry."],[510.94,"We talked about this, was the reason I pointed us back to Leviticus 16."],[514.14,"We talked about the day of atonement really being directed towards that."],[518.22,"Once a year we go and we purify the holy space of all that."],[522.95,"All that residue, all that, all that taint, all that spore left behind, by the sinful people, the sinful use of it."],[530.33,"That's what this is talking about."],[532.49,"That's what this is talking about."],[534.25,"And it's saying, This is your responsibility."],[539.93,"So we've now established the authority of Aaron and his sons in his house."],[541.61,"authority Thatity comes with responsibil."],[542.09,"That's how they're related"],[549.41,"So the fact that you have this authority, the fact that you have this privilege of being the ones who go in there and serve, as we've now established, just you and nobody else, means you have this responsibility now for the purity, the holiness, of this space and yourselves when you're going and entering in."],[567.91,"Verse 2 you shall also bring your brethren, the tribe of Levi, the tribe of your father, to yourself, and they shall be joined and added to you and minister liturgically with you and your sons with you before the tabernacle of testimony."],[581.83,"We talked about, we saw that the tribe of the Levites, the different clans, and had their own. assigned responsibilities, to assist them"],[590.21,"They shall perform your guard duties and the duties of the tabernacle, but they shall not come near the holy vessels and the altar lest they die, they and you also."],[599.89,"They shall be joined to you and perform the guard duties of the tabernacle of testimony and all the liturgical services of the tabernacle, but an outsider shall not come near you."],[609.01,"So we talked about back then when we were talking about the Levites, how they're connected to the idea of deacons, in our current church arrangement."],[619.43,"So they're in this space where they're not lay people, but they're also not priests."],[627.6,"So they have their own ministry, their own assigned ministry, and they're not to try to intrude on and take for themselves."],[634.14,"The ministry of the priests that isn't theirs, but also lay people aren't to encroach on what belongs to them."],[643.02,"So as we saw, not just each group, priest, high priest, priests, Levites, but even the individual families and clans that have their assigned jobs that they're to do."],[653.82,"They're not to try to grasp for other ones that aren't theirs."],[657.44,"And nobody's supposed to try to take theirs away from them."],[660.56,"We just had this Korah episode."],[662.26,"So we're reiterating all of this."],[665.46,"Thus you shall perform the guard duties of the holy things in the altar, so there be may be no more wrath on the children of Israel."],[673.62,"We just saw these episodes of God's wrath of the fire coming out."],[674.58,"Round opening up, all these things"],[680.12,"That was sort of Nadab and Abahu, but on a much bigger scale."],[683.4,"And notice how it's described."],[685.08,"They keep using this guard duties because one of their responsibilities is to protect the holiness of holy places."],[696.2,"To keep things that are holy and sacred, holy and sacred and set apart."],[701.09,"Make sure they don't get common use."],[703.57,"Make sure that people don't come in further than they should."],[707.91,"If they're not supposed to."],[709.35,"And this is not protecting God from those people."],[712.47,"God's not worried about that."],[713.83,"It's protecting these people from God, kind of, in the sense of. protecting them from bringing judgment upon themselves"],[723.41,"This is something that we see St."],[725.73,"Paul in 1 Corinthians, when he's talking about the Eucharist."],[729.05,"He talks about people who receive unworthily, and some of you have gotten sick, and some of you have died because you've drawn close to God in an unworthy way."],[738.09,"As I always reiterate about that, worthy and unworthy, it's not an adjective."],[742.25,"It's not that there's worthy people and unworthy people, it's an adverb."],[747.13,"They approach unworthily."],[748.81,"It's about how you approach God."],[752.66,"Not some kind of state you're in, but how you are approaching God."],[756.02,"And part of approaching God worth the Lee is approaching in repentance and faithfulness."],[762.06,"So that the person who comes receive communion and tells me, Father, I am worthy to receive communion today, is the last person I'm going to give communion to."],[770.46,"The person who comes and says, I am unworthy."],[772.78,"In fact, you don't get to see behind the altar, but when the priest takes communion himself, he literally pronounces himself unworthy as he does it."],[786.14,"Like you do it after saying that you are unworthy of it."],[790.7,"So it's a question of part of approaching worthily is acknowledging that you're not worthy to receive what God is going to give you."],[798.94,"But this is this is something that a lot of friends who aren't Orthodox don't understand."],[807.76,"They don't understand why they can't just wander into this church and receive the Eucharist."],[813.12,"They don't understand why they can't just wander in here and come back behind the altar."],[817.2,"They don't. Like they they don't have an understanding of that anymore."],[822.54,"But this is deeply ingrained in what is in Scripture."],[828.08,"Is that there are places that are holy because God is presence there, and it is a dangerous thing, to approach God in an unworthy way."],[837.38,"And people need to be protected from right doing the wrong thing."],[843.7,"And the when you are ordained as a priest in the Orthodox Church, the lamb for communion, that liturgy is put in your hands, and you're charged with protecting it, guarding it."],[859.43,"The same kind of language."],[861.75,"Not administering it faithfully, not protecting it, protecting the body of Christ."],[867.83,"That's at multiple levels."],[869.67,"Protecting the body of Christ is in your flock, but also protecting the Eucharist in this sense that you you don't sort of aid and abet people receiving it in an unworthy way that could harm them."],[883.99,"And so this is a big part of their job."],[889.19,"And this is part of what it means that they're held responsible for the people."],[895.55,"Like I talked about last time, part of what comes with authority of the church is also having to give an account to Christ for what you did with that authority."],[907.55,"And so uh part of that is who I give the Eucharist to and who I don't."],[916.83,"Who I tell they need to repent and who I don't."],[920.99,"Yes. I recently had a conversation like this with some Presbyterian friends, and they were saying, why don't why can't we take communion into your charge?"],[929.39,"And I gave them this argument, and they looked at me like I'd lost my mind."],[933.71,"Too bad about Arthur's mind, how the Orthodox corrupted it."],[937.31,"It just absolutely, they could not wrap their heads around it."],[939.47,"Yeah They thought I was nuts."],[942.63,"Yeah. And it's I try with with folks, I tried to go to the Bible with them, and I have found that there people who hold that view, among people who hold that view, no one takes what Paul says in 1 Corinthians seriously."],[960.15,"Because I'll say to them, like, I don't give it to you because you might die."],[964.15,"And they either laugh or they think that's ridiculous."],[968.15,"But I point out, well, that's what St."],[969.75,"Paul says. They say, and they say something flippant like, Well, that's on me then."],[975.91,"You know, and I'm like, Well, that shows me you don't believe it."],[979.03,"Because you would say something flippant like that if you actually believed it was true that you could die."],[983.77,"So I don't know how to get around the fact that they just don't believe Saint Paul."],[991.25,"They just don't believe that part of the scriptures."],[994.13,"The people who hold that view."],[995.73,"And that's not all Presbyterians."],[997.01,"That's not all Calvinists."],[999.17,"There are Calvinists, the Calvinists I grew up among hat practice closed communion."],[1004.39,"Um Lutherans, it's not all, it tends to be sort of low church evangelicals."],[1010.71,"I think it's a denial of the real presence."],[1012.31,"More often. Well, yeah, because because they don't think it actually is anything, they don't understand why, or why or how it could kill you."],[1020.55,"Even though St."],[1021.35,"Paul says that, you"],[1022.33,"And there's not a way around that's what St."],[1024.49,"Paul says. And so they just they don't take that seriously."],[1027.77,"I don't know what to do about that"],[1029.65,"Some somewhere when this episode comes out, when this is released as a podcast, there'll be some angry typing Presbyterian, and it will be like, you know, that's not true."],[1038.05,"Father Stephen is usually right about these things, but now this time he's way off base."],[1042.51,"Uh and explaining why some out of no, we do believe what Paul says, but it won't affect me ever because I'm elect or something, who knows."],[1052.2,"Yeah. But so this is just deeply ingrained in the scriptures."],[1056.52,"There's sort there's sort of not a way around it without denying something in the scriptures."],[1063.16,"Verse 6: Behold, I took your brethren the Levites from the midst of the children of Israel as a gift given to the Lord to minister liturgically in the tabernacle of testimony."],[1072.72,"Therefore, you and your sons with you shall take care of your priesthood according to all the manner of the altar and within the veil, and you shall minister liturgically as the gift of your priesthood, but the outsider who comes near shall be put to death."],[1085.68,"So notice again he's reiterating."],[1112.56,"Now he's talking to those people and saying, Look, this is a gift you've been given."],[1116.5,"And you need to perform it accordingly."],[1120.0,"This is this incredible privilege you have to come before God and offer these sacrifices, to do these things."],[1127.84,"And therefore must be taken seriously."],[1131.6,"Again the Lord spoke to Aaron, I give you charge over the first fruits from all the ch things sanctified to me by the children of Israel, and I give these things to you and your sons with you as your share."],[1142.32,"This shall be an eternal ordinance."],[1144.56,"So let this be yours from the sanctified holy things of the offerings, from all their gifts, from all their sacrifices, from all their trespass offerings, and from all their sin offerings, and from whatever they return to me, let all these holy things belong to you and your sons."],[1159.04,"So we've already read about this is reiterating."],[1161.44,"This is part of what they've been given"],[1164.65,"They're not going to be out there working the fields day in, day out, like everyone else in Israel."],[1170.99,"But they're going to be receiving food, in this way, from the tized offerings of the people."],[1177.16,"In a most holy place, you shall eat these things."],[1182.28,"Every male shall eat these things, it shall be holy to you."],[1185.8,"This also shall be a first fruit for you from their gifts, from all the deposit offerings of the children of Israel."],[1191.72,"I give these things to you and to your sons and daughters with you."],[1195.16,"This shall be an eternal ordinance."],[1197.24,"Every one who is clean in your house shall eat these things, the first fruits of oil, wine, and grain, all their first fruits, whatever they may offer to the Lord, I give these things to you."],[1204.52,"to the Lord. Whatever first ripe fruit is in their land, which they bring shall be yours"],[1212.08,"Everyone who is clean in your house shall eat these things."],[1214.64,"Every devoted thing in Israel shall be yours."],[1218.16,"So this is another part of the privilege they have is that you're not going to be out there toiling the same way other people are."],[1226.72,"You're going to be supported, but you're going to be supported so that you can focus on doing this ministry."],[1232.98,"And so this is the this is the paradigm that Saint Paul in particular brings forward the New Testament in terms of leadership within Christian communities."],[1242.42,"The idea that the community should support those leaders so that they can devote themselves to the. ministry God has given them"],[1254.06,"I tell people, and this is how the church has always seen it, that I do not have a job."],[1261.5,"Being a priest is not a job."],[1265.12,"Like a normal job."],[1266.96,"It is neither contract labor nor wage labor."],[1271.42,"It is not a job."],[1273.82,"I am supported by the community so that I don't have to get a job."],[1278.7,"So that I can devote myself to doing the things of the priesthood."],[1283.34,"This is how God set it up originally"],[1283.64,"And this is where that comes from."],[1287.57,"There are these special tasks related to the priesthood that have to be done."],[1291.45,"In order for people to be able to focus on that and do that, and do that in any kind of worthy way, they can't also be trying to manage a farm and a household and a business and all these other things on the side."],[1305.77,"Also, was that Mars Rebellion is that you probably just wanted to get out of labor?"],[1309.93,"Well, we don't know."],[1311.53,"We don't know what his sort of end game was."],[1320.73,"Well, so uh I think I think we ought yeah, we saw back when they were talking about the Levites that there were uh, I mean, for the most part, they're the wives and right daughters of other Levites."],[1334.73,"Of course, wives, they're doing all the things wives did in terms of a household."],[1337.93,"Um managing the house"],[1344.02,"Yes, yeah, no, they those things were kept within the that's really good."],[1348.26,"Yeah, yeah, yeah."],[1349.46,"But also uh we saw the the women at the gates of the tabernacle that there were women, uh usually widows, minority of women probably who never got married for some reason, um who did things for the tabernacle, like sewing and repairing vestments and all of those kind of things."],[1371.06,"So there were those women from among the Levites had filled that special role, and that evolves into the women at the temple."],[1381.86,"So like the Theotoko Slater."],[1384.48,"That institution of having those women who are dedicated to God's service came from the Levite women here in the Torah."],[1394.1,"Over time. Once you eventually you get a temple, so you're not at the gate of the tabernacle anymore, and the temple has temple courts and other areas."],[1402.52,"But down the down the chain, that's where that uh ends up."],[1408.44,"Everything that first opens the womb of all flesh, which they bring to the Lord from man to cattle, shall be yours."],[1416.04,"Nevertheless, the firstborn of men you shall redeem, and the firstborn of unclean cattle you shall redeem."],[1423.08,"There is for its redemption at the age of one month. the rate is five shekels according to the holy shekel, that is twenty oboe"],[1431.44,"These are weights."],[1433.21,"And so we have no precise but it's referred to as the holy shekel because there would be some weight that was kept at the tabernacle."],[1442.47,"Because we're talking about balance scales."],[1445.49,"And so, well, no, there was no universal shekel, that's the point."],[1449.09,"So it's here's the tabernacle shekel."],[1452.47,"And it weighs 20 oboes."],[1454.63,"But what's a scientific oboe?"],[1456.55,"Well, it's one twentieth of a shekel."],[1458.44,"And so that would be put in the balance weight."],[1462.05,"On the one side of the balance scale, and then you'd put whatever on the other side to determine, oh, that's a shekel worth."],[1468.49,"Now, this is giving more detail, because we actually already saw this."],[1473.11,"That the offering of the firstborn was described, remember, because there's the whole issue of the donkey, or like an unclean that's what it means by unclean cattle."],[1479.51,"The word that's translated cattle here didn't just mean cows, it meant sort of beasts of the field."],[1485.51,"So it was sort of a wider range."],[1488.95,"So a donkey would be an example of unclean cattle."],[1492.31,"A horse would be an example of unclean cattle."],[1495.27,"Anything that didn't have, as we saw in Leviticus, a cloven hoof and eat cud, that's would be unclean."],[1504.55,"But still, as a domesticated animal, the firstborn male would be dedicated to God."],[1510.55,"And we were told, well, if it's one that you don't sacrifice, or if it's a human, you redeem it."],[1512.87,"And so this is giving the sort of redemption values what that means if you can't."],[1521.29,"And this is going to become especially important."],[1523.61,"We're getting this later."],[1525.23,"This detail later, because this is going to become especially important once they come into the land."],[1529.55,"Because you're not necessarily, even with something you could sacrifice like a sheep, you're not necessarily going to be able to drag the sheep from where you live up in Bashan or on the other side of the Jordan River over to Jerusalem."],[1542.05,"And so in order to make that effective."],[1545.5,"And you're not going to be allowed to perform sacrifices back where you were."],[1548.98,"So easy way to do that is you come to Jerusalem, you give the redemption value to the to the temple."],[1557.22,"And this is talking about how that's calculated."],[1560.98,"But the firstborn of young bulls, the firstborn of sheep, or the firstborn of goats, you shall not redeem, they are holy, you shall pour out their blood towards the altar, and offer their fat as a burnt offering for a sweet aroma to the Lord."],[1572.5,"Their meat shall also be yours, just as the breast of the deposit offering and the right shoulder are yours."],[1578.18,"Every choice part of the holy things which the children of Israel offer to the Lord, I give to you and your sons and daughters with you as an eternal ordinance."],[1587.14,"It is an eternal covenant of salt before the Lord with you and your seed with you."],[1592.1,"Salt has to do with the sacrifices."],[1593.96,"Remember, they add salt to all the sacrifices."],[1597.56,"So what's being outlined here is you have these privileges, you have these responsibilities, you have these duties, you have these benefits."],[1610.69,"This is sort of the life that's been given to you, as a priest."],[1615.27,"It's a contract."],[1616.39,"Yeah. Um, or a covenant, yeah."],[1619.66,"And notice this is not like God's not negotiating."],[1623.74,"And number two, they've already received it."],[1626.7,"They've received the priesthood."],[1628.14,"We read about them receiving the priesthood."],[1629.58,"It's been right."],[1630.7,"And God has now said, here's what this entails."],[1635.52,"And also, there is implied here, you should be satisfied with this."],[1641.76,"That's part of what this is about."],[1642.56,"You're gonna have all the food you need and good food"],[1648.48,"With the number of sacrifices and stuff and the size of Israel, they're gonna be eating a lot more meat than any other tribe."],[1655.04,"Farmers don't eat a lot of meat."],[1656.72,"They're eating more eat, they're eating better."],[1658.72,"They're gonna be right."],[1659.6,"So, I mean, this is but be satisfied with it in the sense that none of these priests or Levites should be trying to get rich."],[1667.76,"We're gonna see this is gonna become a pernicious problem throughout the rest of the Old Testament and into the New Testament."],[1673.76,"We've talked about the high priest family owning incredible amounts of land and basically swindling it out of the people."],[1680.72,"There's gonna be this temptation to."],[1684.18,"First, God said, don't. grasp for more responsibilities and duties and privileges that haven't been given to you"],[1691.18,"Also, now here."],[1692.74,"Be satisfied with all of this."],[1695.08,"And don't try and grasp for more."],[1697.64,"Ambition is not a virtue."],[1702.28,"This is hard for Americans to accept."],[1705.34,"We consider people who aren't ambitious lazy."],[1709.66,"We consider contentment to be kind of a vice."],[1713.5,"But that's the opposite of what God says."],[1717.9,"God says contentment is a virtue."],[1720.86,"God says ambition is a vice."],[1724.46,"Constantly wanting more."],[1726.86,"More power, more money, more authority, more control, more stuff, is a vi is bad."],[1729.82,"Is sinful Competing with other people for those things is sinful."],[1741.08,"Sorry, Americans. Contentment, being happy with what you have."],[1748.52,"Being happy with what God has given you."],[1750.52,"Being happy with the life God has given you."],[1753.32,"Being satisfied are good things."],[1756.2,"These are good things."],[1757.24,"We talked about this before back when St."],[1758.84,"Paul said that we should be praying to lead a quiet and peaceful life in godliness and sanctity."],[1764.76,"That should be our goal."],[1766.44,"Not a lot of people's goal these days, living a quiet and peaceful life off by themselves."],[1772.6,"But that's what God says we should aspire to."],[1774.36,"And that's what He's trying to communicate to the priests"],[1780.88,"Got a lot of responsibility, that's a heavy thing."],[1783.52,"You've also got a lot of gifts and privileges."],[1786.0,"And so you should be happy right with this."],[1789.6,"And fulfill those duties and responsibilities."],[1793.28,"Moreover, the Lord said to Aaron, You shall have no inheritance in their land, nor shall you have any portion among them."],[1800.24,"I am your portion and your inheritance in the midst of the children of Israel."],[1805.04,"So remember, we already talked about this."],[1806.72,"They're not going to get the land allotments because they're not going to be there working and farming the land."],[1811.92,"God is their inheritance."],[1813.76,"I used to joke, but people didn't get it."],[1815.84,"I used to joke that being a priest doesn't have a lot of benefits, but it has a great retirement plan."],[1820.76,"And people thought I was talking about an actual retirement plan."],[1823.8,"I am not."],[1824.44,"We do not have a great actual retirement plan."],[1827.56,"We don't have much of any actual retirement plan."],[1831.16,"But I was referring to heaven."],[1837.48,"Which hopefully, as a priest, we're shooting for at least."],[1841.24,"But that's the idea."],[1842.12,"That's what God is saying here when he says he is their inheritance."],[1845.42,"Meaning you shouldn't be trying to accumulate wealth in this world."],[1849.58,"You have these privileges, you have God."],[1852.46,"That's better than wealth at a big farm and land and cattle."],[1859.66,"Behold, I give the children of Levi all the tithes in Israel as an inheritance. in return for their liturgical service"],[1866.74,"Whenever they minister liturgically in the tabernacle of testimony, hereafter the children of Israel shall not come near the tabernacle of testimony, lest they bear guilt and die."],[1876.58,"But the Levite himself shall minister liturgically in the tabernacle of testimony, and they shall bear their sins."],[1882.58,"It shall be an eternal ordinance throughout your generations that in the midst of the children of Israel they shall have no inheritance."],[1890.34,"Clearly, once again, the Levites are not being punished for everyone else's sins."],[1896.02,"This bearing them means they're going in and making the offerings for the sins of the people."],[1901.86,"The people themselves are not going in there."],[1904.34,"right But the Levites are going in on their behalf."],[1907.31,"behalf. Makes you think Isaiah 53 might be talking about Christ doing something on our"],[1914.39,"But we'll get to Isaiah eventually."],[1917.83,"For the tithes of the children of Israel, whatever they may offer as a choice portion to the Lord, I give to the Levites as an inheritance."],[1924.23,"Therefore I say to them, in the midst of the children of Israel, they shall have no inheritance."],[1928.79,"Then the Lord spoke to Moses, saying, Speak thus to the Levites and say to them, If you receive from the children of Israel the tithe, which I give you from them as your inheritance, then you shall remove from it the Lord's choice portion, a tenth of the tithe."],[1942.15,"Now your choice portions shall be reckoned to you as the grain from the threshing floor, it is the choice portion of the wine press."],[1949.27,"Thus you shall then remove the Lord's choice portions from all your tithes. whatever you might receive from the children of Israel, and you shall give from them the Lord's choice portion to Aaron the priest"],[1959.87,"From all your gifts you shall remove the choice portion for the Lord, or from all the first fruits, that which is sanctified from it."],[1967.23,"So this is interesting."],[1969.71,"So God has said, you're going to be receiving the tithes from the other Israelites."],[1974.29,"That doesn't mean that the priests and the Levites are like just immune from, oh, you don't have to offer God anything yourselves."],[1985.41,"They do too."],[1986.71,"So they're taking a tithe from the tithes."],[1989.19,"And notice it's specifically grain and wine."],[1993.75,"But those are that's what they then offer."],[1997.03,"And Aaron is the high priest"],[1999.65,"The high priest then offers on behalf of the priests and the Levites."],[2007.25,"So this is talking about the relationship within the Old Testament clergy."],[2014.53,"And this is pretty much paralleled in the Orthodox Church with the relationship between priests and deacons and then the bishop."],[2023.25,"Therefore, you shall say to them, When you remove the first fruit from it, then all the rest shall be accounted to the Levites as the produce of the threshing floor and as the produce of the wine press."],[2032.69,"You may eat it in any place, you and your households, for it is your reward for your liturgical service in the tabernacle of testimony."],[2039.81,"Now you should bear no guilt because of it, for you removed the first root from it."],[2044.09,"You shall not defile the holy things of the children of Israel lest you die."],[2048.33,"Meaning he's making a distinction between their tithes, those offerings, and the sacrificial offerings."],[2055.93,"So they have to eat the whatever they have to eat the sacrificial offerings, their part of the sacrifices in a holy place."],[2062.49,"But just the tithes from Israel, they could eat wherever."],[2067.29,"That's the idea there."],[2068.97,"Because and the reason they can eat them anywhere is they've already removed God's part."],[2073.93,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2081.21,"Father Stephen's email address is whole counsel at ancient faith.com."],[2086.41,"That's whole.counsel at ancientfaith.com"]],"o":[{"t":23.52,"lv":2,"h":"Shifting gears: from story to duties","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Starting <b>Numbers 18</b> - \"exciting book of Numbers\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Shifting <b>content type</b> again</li><li class=\"d1\">last time: <b>narrative</b> - Korah's rebellion, plague, censers</li><li class=\"d1\">repeats Korah = \"first Protestant\" joke - \"won't stop me\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Rebellion, ground swallowing, <b>Aaron's rod</b> budding → firmly established</li><li class=\"d1\">high priest authority <b>given by God</b>, not taken</li><li class=\"d1\">\"no one can seize it\" - only legitimate way is <b>God gives it</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Tonight: review <b>duties of the priests and Levites</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>responsibilities</b> that come with the authority</li><li class=\"d1\">not narrative; <b>not progressing the story</b></li><li class=\"d0\">No <b>real-time narration</b>: 40 years announced; at end of Numbers it's <b>40 years later</b></li><li class=\"d1\">when narrative resumes, doesn't pick up where it left off</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>windows</b>\" onto important events over the 40 years</li><li class=\"d1\">whole years with no inkling; the <b>life of the community</b> goes on, <b>punctuated</b> by major events</li></ul>"},{"t":239.6,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 18:1 - \"Bearing the sins of the holy things\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>18:1</b> Aaron, sons, father's house \"<b>bear the sins</b> of the holy things\" and \"of your priesthood\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Bear sins\" ≠ \"get punished\"</li><li class=\"d1\">some friends read <b>Isaiah 53</b> (servant bearing our sins) = <b>God punished Jesus</b></li><li class=\"d1\">same language in the <b>Torah</b> makes no sense that way</li><li class=\"d1\">punished for sins of <b>inanimate objects</b>? <b>double punished</b>? \"Obviously doesn't make sense\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Back to <b>Leviticus 16</b>: different understanding of sin</li><li class=\"d1\">we think: <b>trespass</b>, rule broken → guilty → <b>liable to punishment</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"That's not the Bible, to be blunt\"</li><li class=\"d1\">sin = a <b>force active in the world</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Genesis 4</b>, Cain: \"sin is <b>crouching at your door</b>, wants to master you\"</li></ul>"},{"t":427.1,"lv":3,"h":"Sin as disease, sins as symptoms","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Sin</b> singular = the force; <b>sins</b> plural = <b>effects</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"if sin is the disease, sins are the <b>symptoms</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Like a <b>spore</b> (no germ theory, but they understood)</li><li class=\"d1\">objects <b>contaminated</b>; disease spreads</li><li class=\"d1\">person's blanket, possessions - <b>burn</b> them</li><li class=\"d1\">two OT examples: <b>plague/disease</b> and <b>mildew/mold</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Candlestand, altar didn't \"break a rule\" - they get <b>tainted by sinful people</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the priests themselves <b>manifest</b> the symptoms, handle the things over their ministry</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Day of Atonement</b> (Lev. 16): once a year <b>purify the holy space</b></li><li class=\"d1\">all the <b>residue, taint, spore</b> left by sinful people</li><li class=\"d0\">\"This is your <b>responsibility</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">authority established → comes with <b>responsibility</b> for <b>purity, holiness</b> of the space and themselves</li></ul>"},{"t":567.91,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 18:2-5 - Levites as guards","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>18:2</b> Bring your brethren the <b>tribe of Levi</b> - joined to you, minister liturgically <b>with</b> you</li><li class=\"d0\">They do <b>guard duties</b> and tabernacle duties</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not</b> come near the holy vessels and altar <b>lest they die, they and you</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"an outsider shall not come near you\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Levites ≈ <b>deacons</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not lay people, not priests</b></li><li class=\"d1\">own assigned ministry - not to take priests'</li><li class=\"d1\">lay people not to <b>encroach</b> on theirs</li><li class=\"d0\">Not just each group - <b>individual families and clans</b> have assigned jobs</li><li class=\"d1\">don't grasp others', nobody takes theirs - \"just had this <b>Korah</b> episode\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>18:5</b> Guard duties of holy things and altar → \"<b>no more wrath</b> on the children of Israel\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Korah episodes = \"<b>Nadab and Abihu on a much bigger scale</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":685.08,"lv":3,"h":"Guarding the holy: protecting people from God","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Duty: <b>protect the holiness</b> of holy places</li><li class=\"d1\">keep holy things set apart, <b>no common use</b></li><li class=\"d1\">don't let people come further than they should</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Not</b> protecting God from people</li><li class=\"d1\">protecting <b>people from God</b> - from bringing <b>judgment on themselves</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1 Corinthians</b> on the Eucharist: receive <b>unworthily</b> - some <b>sick, some died</b></li><li class=\"d1\">worthy/unworthy = <b>adverb</b>, not adjective - <b>how you approach</b></li><li class=\"d1\">approach in <b>repentance and faithfulness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I am worthy to receive today\" = <b>last person</b> I'll give it to</li><li class=\"d1\">priest <b>pronounces himself unworthy</b> at his own communion</li><li class=\"d1\">worthily = acknowledging you're <b>not worthy</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Non-Orthodox don't see why they can't <b>wander in, receive, go behind the altar</b></li><li class=\"d1\">but it's <b>deeply ingrained in Scripture</b>: places holy because of <b>God's presence</b> → <b>dangerous</b> to approach unworthily</li><li class=\"d0\">Ordination: the <b>Lamb</b> is put in your hands - charged to <b>guard</b> it</li><li class=\"d1\">same language - protect the <b>body of Christ</b>: <b>flock</b> and the <b>Eucharist</b></li><li class=\"d1\">don't <b>aid and abet</b> unworthy reception that could harm</li><li class=\"d1\">held <b>responsible</b> - give account to Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">who I give the Eucharist to, who I tell to repent</li></ul>"},{"t":920.99,"lv":3,"h":"Q: Presbyterian friends and closed communion","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Presbyterian friends: why can't we take communion in your charge?</li><li class=\"d1\">gave this argument - \"looked at me like I'd lost my mind\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"thought I was nuts\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Go to the Bible: <b>no one</b> who holds that view takes <b>1 Cor.</b> seriously</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I don't give it to you because you <b>might die</b>\" - they laugh</li><li class=\"d1\">reply: \"that's on me then\" - flippant → \"<b>you don't believe it</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"they just don't believe Saint Paul\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not all Presbyterians or Calvinists</li><li class=\"d1\">Calvinists he grew up among <b>practiced closed communion</b>; Lutherans too</li><li class=\"d1\">tends to be <b>low church evangelicals</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Q: denial of the <b>real presence</b>? A: yes - think it isn't anything, can't see how it could kill you</li><li class=\"d0\">Expect \"angry typing Presbyterian\" - \"I'm <b>elect</b>, so it won't affect me\"</li><li class=\"d0\">No way around it <b>without denying something in Scripture</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1063.16,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 18:6-13 - The priests' portion","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>18:6-7</b> Levites = a <b>gift</b> given to the Lord to minister</li><li class=\"d1\">you and sons: priesthood, <b>altar</b> and <b>within the veil</b>; <b>outsider</b> who comes near put to death</li><li class=\"d1\">a <b>gift</b> and incredible privilege → <b>take seriously</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>18:8-10</b> Charge over <b>first fruits</b>, sanctified things → your share, <b>eternal ordinance</b></li><li class=\"d1\">from gifts, sacrifices, <b>trespass</b> and <b>sin offerings</b></li><li class=\"d1\">eat in a <b>most holy place</b>; every male eats</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>18:11-13</b> Also first fruits - <b>oil, wine, grain</b>, first ripe fruit</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>sons and daughters</b>; everyone <b>clean</b> in the house eats</li><li class=\"d1\">every <b>devoted thing</b> in Israel is yours</li><li class=\"d0\">Not out <b>working the fields</b> like everyone else</li><li class=\"d1\">supported from the <b>tithed offerings</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1218.16,"lv":3,"h":"Q: Support for ministry - \"priesthood is not a job\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Not toiling like others - <b>supported so they can focus on ministry</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>paradigm St. Paul</b> brings in NT for leadership</li><li class=\"d1\">community supports leaders to <b>devote themselves</b> to ministry</li><li class=\"d0\">\"I do not have a <b>job</b>\" - neither <b>contract</b> nor <b>wage</b> labor</li><li class=\"d1\">supported by the community <b>so I don't have to get a job</b></li><li class=\"d1\">how God set it up; special tasks → can't also manage <b>farm, household, business</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Q: was Korah's rebellion just wanting to <b>get out of labor</b>? A: don't know his <b>end game</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Q: Levite <b>women</b>? A: wives and daughters</li><li class=\"d1\">wives: <b>household</b> as any wife</li><li class=\"d1\">also <b>women at the gates of the tabernacle</b>: usually <b>widows</b>, minority never married</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>sewing, repairing vestments</b></li><li class=\"d1\">evolves into <b>women at the temple</b> → <b>Theotokos</b> serving there</li><li class=\"d1\">institution of women dedicated to God's service comes from <b>Levite women</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1408.44,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 18:15-19 - Firstborn and redemption","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>18:15-16</b> Firstborn of all flesh, man to cattle, yours</li><li class=\"d1\">firstborn of <b>men redeemed</b>; firstborn of <b>unclean cattle</b> redeemed</li><li class=\"d1\">at <b>one month</b>: <b>five shekels</b>, \"holy shekel\" = <b>20 gerahs</b> (oboes)</li><li class=\"d0\">Weights, <b>balance scales</b> - <b>no universal shekel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"tabernacle shekel\" - weight kept at the tabernacle</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>oboe</b> (gerah) = <b>1/20</b> of a shekel; weight on one side, goods on the other</li><li class=\"d0\">More detail on <b>firstborn</b> already seen</li><li class=\"d1\">\"cattle\" = <b>beasts of the field</b>, wider range</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>donkey</b>, <b>horse</b> = unclean cattle - no <b>cloven hoof and chew cud</b> (Leviticus)</li><li class=\"d1\">domesticated firstborn male dedicated to God; human or non-sacrificable → <b>redeem</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Matters <b>later</b> in the land</li><li class=\"d1\">can't drag a sheep from <b>Bashan</b> or across the <b>Jordan</b> to Jerusalem</li><li class=\"d1\">sacrifices only at one place → give <b>redemption value</b> to the temple</li><li class=\"d1\">this = how it's calculated</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>18:17-19</b> Firstborn of <b>bulls, sheep, goats</b> not redeemed - <b>holy</b></li><li class=\"d1\">blood poured at the altar, fat burnt - <b>sweet aroma</b></li><li class=\"d1\">meat yours, like the <b>breast</b> and <b>right shoulder</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>covenant of salt</b>\" - salt added to all sacrifices</li></ul>"},{"t":1597.56,"lv":2,"h":"Be satisfied: contentment, not ambition","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Privileges, responsibilities, duties, benefits = <b>the life given to you as a priest</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Q: a contract? A: <b>covenant</b> - God <b>not negotiating</b>; already received the priesthood, now \"here's what it entails\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Implied: <b>be satisfied</b> - all the food you need, <b>good food</b></li><li class=\"d1\">many sacrifices, size of Israel → <b>more meat</b> than any other tribe</li><li class=\"d1\">\"farmers don't eat a lot of meat\"</li><li class=\"d0\">But <b>not to get rich</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>pernicious problem</b> through OT and NT: high priest family owning <b>land</b>, swindling it from the people</li><li class=\"d1\">first: don't grasp for <b>more responsibilities, privileges</b>; now: <b>be satisfied</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Ambition is not a virtue</b>\" - hard for Americans</li><li class=\"d1\">we call unambitious people <b>lazy</b>, contentment a <b>vice</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God: <b>contentment = virtue</b>, <b>ambition = vice</b></li><li class=\"d1\">constantly wanting <b>more power, money, authority, control, stuff</b> = sinful</li><li class=\"d1\">competing with others for it = sinful - \"Sorry, Americans\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Be happy with what God gave, the <b>life</b> he gave</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul: pray for a <b>quiet and peaceful life</b> in godliness and sanctity</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Not a lot of people's goal these days\" - but that's what God says to aspire to</li></ul>"},{"t":1793.28,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 18:20-24 - God as inheritance; the tithe","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>18:20</b> \"<b>No inheritance</b> in their land... <b>I am your portion and your inheritance</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">no land allotments - not there farming</li><li class=\"d1\">joke: priesthood \"doesn't have many benefits but a <b>great retirement plan</b>\" - <b>heaven</b>, not an actual plan</li><li class=\"d1\">don't accumulate <b>wealth</b> in this world - God \"better than a big farm, land and cattle\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>18:21</b> Levites get <b>all the tithes</b> in Israel in return for <b>liturgical service</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Israelites not to come near the tabernacle <b>lest they bear guilt and die</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Levites \"<b>bear their sins</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Levites <b>not punished</b> for others' sins</li><li class=\"d1\">bearing = going in and <b>making the offerings</b> for the people's sins</li><li class=\"d1\">people don't go in; Levites go <b>on their behalf</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"Makes you think <b>Isaiah 53</b> might be talking about Christ doing something on our behalf\" - \"we'll get to Isaiah eventually\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1928.79,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 18:25-32 - The tithe of the tithe","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>18:25-26</b> Levites remove the Lord's <b>choice portion</b>, <b>a tenth of the tithe</b></li><li class=\"d1\">give it to <b>Aaron the priest</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Priests and Levites <b>not immune</b> - they also offer</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>tithe from the tithes</b></li><li class=\"d1\">specifically <b>grain and wine</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>high priest</b> offers on behalf of priests and Levites</li><li class=\"d0\">Parallel in Orthodox Church: <b>priests, deacons, then the bishop</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>18:30-32</b> After the first fruit is removed, the rest = <b>reward for liturgical service</b></li><li class=\"d1\">eat it <b>in any place</b>, with households</li><li class=\"d1\">\"shall not defile the holy things... lest you die\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Distinction: <b>tithes</b> vs. <b>sacrificial offerings</b></li><li class=\"d1\">sacrificial portions eaten in a <b>holy place</b></li><li class=\"d1\">tithes eaten <b>anywhere</b> - <b>God's part already removed</b></li></ul>"}]});
